    <statement><p>Let <m>f</m> and <m>g</m> be the functions defined by <m>f(t) = 2t^{2}</m> and <m>g(t) = t^{3}+4t</m>.</p>
<p>a. Determine <m>f'(t)</m> and <m>g'(t)</m>.</p>
<p><m>f'(t) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>g'(t) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>b. Let <m>p(t) = 2t^{2} (t^{3}+4t)</m> and observe that <m>p(t) = f(t) \cdot g(t)</m>. Rewrite the formula
for <m>p</m> by distributing the <m>2t^{2}</m> term. Once you do this, you will have the sum of 2 terms, and you can enter them in either order below.</p>
<p><m>p(t)=</m><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0003"/> <m>+</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
<p>Then, compute <m>p'(t)</m> using the sum and constant
multiple rules.</p>
<p><m>p'(t) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
<p>c. Calculate <m>f'(t)\cdot g'(t) =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0006"/></p>
<p>True or False: <m>p'(t) = f'(t) \cdot g'(t)</m>
<ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0007"><li>
<p>?</p>
</li><li>
<p>True</p>
</li><li>
<p>False</p>
</li></ul></p>
<p>d. Let <m>q(t) = \displaystyle{\frac{t^{3}+4t}{2t^{2}}}</m> and observe that <m>q(t) = \displaystyle{\frac{g(t)}{f(t)}}</m>. 
Rewrite the formula
for <m>q</m> by dividing each term in the numerator by the denominator and simplify to write <m>q(t)</m>
as a sum of constant multiples of powers of <m>t</m>. Once you do this, you will have the sum of 2 terms, and you can enter them in either order below.</p>
<p><m>q(t)=</m><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0008"/> <m>+</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0009"/></p>
<p>Then, compute <m>q'(t)</m> using the sum and constant
multiple rules.</p>
<p><m>q'(t) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0010"/></p>
<p>e. Calculate <m>\frac{g'(t)}{f'(t)} =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0011"/></p>
<p>True or False: <m>q'(t) = \displaystyle{\frac{g'(t)}{f'(t)}}</m>
<ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0012"><li>
<p>?</p>
</li><li>
<p>True</p>
</li><li>
<p>False</p>
</li></ul></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
